
<section class="page-content">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="reveal">
      <h2>Where it began</h2>
      <p>Aura & Oak started in 2019 in a converted garage in Portland, Oregon. Our founder, Elena, had spent a decade in industrial design before a chance encounter with a small-batch candle maker in Kyoto changed everything. The way a single scent could transform a room — could transform a <em>feeling</em> — felt like a revelation.</p>
      <p>She came home with a notebook full of ideas and a suitcase full of wax samples. Six months later, the first candle — Amber & Oakmoss — was poured. Not in a factory. Not on an assembly line. By hand, on a wooden table, with a copper pitcher and a thermometer.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-split reveal" style="margin:64px 0">
      <div class="page-split-media reveal-clip">
        {%- if section.settings.image_url != blank -%}
          <img src="{{ section.settings.image_url }}" alt="Studio" loading="lazy">
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      <div class="page-split-content">
        <span class="eyebrow">The studio</span>
        <h2>Still small. Still by hand.</h2>
        <p>Seven years later, we're still a team of nine. We still pour every candle by hand. We still source our soy wax from American farms, our fragrances from independent perfumers in Grasse, and our ceramic vessels from a family-run studio in Portland's Alberta district.</p>
        <p>We've grown, but we haven't scaled. There's a difference.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="reveal">The timeline</h2>
    <div class="timeline stagger">
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <div class="timeline-year">2019</div>
          <h4>The first pour</h4>
          <p>Amber & Oakmoss debuts at the Portland Saturday Market. We sell 23 candles in a single day.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-dot"></div>
        <div class="timeline-spacer"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-spacer"></div>
        <div class="timeline-dot"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <div class="timeline-year">2020</div>
          <h4>The ceramic collaboration</h4>
          <p>We partner with studio potter James Okabe to create our signature hand-thrown vessels.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <div class="timeline-year">2021</div>
          <h4>The diffuser line</h4>
          <p>Launching our ceramic reed diffusers — designed to live on your shelf long after the scent fades.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-dot"></div>
        <div class="timeline-spacer"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-spacer"></div>
        <div class="timeline-dot"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <div class="timeline-year">2023</div>
          <h4>The studio expands</h4>
          <p>We move into a 3,000 sq ft workshop in the Pearl District. Same wooden table. More room to pour.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <div class="timeline-year">2025</div>
          <h4>The ritual journal</h4>
          <p>We launch our editorial platform — essays, interviews, and guides on mindful living.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-dot"></div>
        <div class="timeline-spacer"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="reveal">What we believe</h2>
    <div class="values-grid stagger">
      <div class="value-card">
        <div class="value-card-icon">✦</div>
        <h4>Craft over scale</h4>
        <p>Every product is made by hand in small batches. We'd rather make less, and make it well, than mass-produce something that loses its soul.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card">
        <div class="value-card-icon">◐</div>
        <h4>Natural materials</h4>
        <p>100% soy wax. Phthalate-free fragrances. Cotton wicks. Ceramic vessels. We choose materials that are kind to your home and the planet.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card">
        <div class="value-card-icon">◈</div>
        <h4>Designed to live on</h4>
        <p>Our vessels are made to be refilled, repurposed, or simply kept. Nothing we make is designed for the landfill.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card">
        <div class="value-card-icon">✧</div>
        <h4>Slow by intention</h4>
        <p>We release two collections a year. Not because we can't make more, but because good things take time — and we'd rather wait than rush.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

